WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Welcome back.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:04.938
-I'm actually more used to
sitting here across from you

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.706 size:81% position:41%
than I am seeing you
out in the real world.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-It's strange.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.609
-It's very strange, yeah,
because we've been lucky enough

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
to run into each other in
the real world,

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.079 size:81% position:41% line:92%
but it's been a while.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.047 line:92%
But you did -- you actually got

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
to hang out with
my son this summer.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:16.916 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Ashe.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.819
-Yeah, because you and Mary are
friends with my in-laws.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you were at
a sporting event

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.758 size:78% position:39%
that my wife brought
my 2-year-old son to.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pig racing.
-Pig racing.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:28.194 size:78% position:39% line:92%
This is a true thing.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:33.233
-Yeah, mini pigs.
Like, many mini pigs in a race.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:37.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they even had a trough
that had water in it.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they'd race a couple times,
then jump in and swim.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:46.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the motivation was
a plate -- true -- of Oreos.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:46.713 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Really?

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.182
That's how you get a pig to run?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:52.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, so, do they
run around a track? A lap?

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Once.
-Okay.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it's like,
"And they're off!"

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.491 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Wasn't that great?"

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So that seems like --
-But let's go back to Ashe.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-What a wonderful young man.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:03.630 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Wonderful young man.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.631 line:92%
And I will tell you, though,

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's a wonderful kid
and I love him,

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he told me
about the pig race,

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there were almost none
of those details.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
As a 2-year-old,
basically all he could tell me

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
was they were pigs.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You want to know why?
-Why?

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:16.943 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Because he blocked it.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:20.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because to be entertaining
with such a short race,

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:24.684
the guy who had the pigs made up
all these horrible names,

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
like Baco Bits and
Little Bacon Running,

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.190 line:92%
you know, and things like that.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm sure it just,
you know, horrified him.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, 'cause that's
a real reminder

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:36.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the children there that
these will eventually be food.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.263 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.166
-"And, by the way, we're eating
all of them, even the winner.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:44.037
Like, nobody can run their way
out of their fates here, yeah."

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.738 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oreo-basted pig.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:46.573 line:92%
-If you taste a piece of bacon

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:50.243
that has a little bit of Oreo
in it, that was your winner.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.879 line:92%
Yeah, that was your winner.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, any one of
the Emmys is a winner,

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.818 size:75% position:38%
so I don't want this
to be hard on you,

00:01:58.818 --> 00:01:59.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you were nominated
for an Emmy.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was good.
I almost believed that.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so,
you were at the Emmys.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.226 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, I was.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:09.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nominated for your work on
"The Good Place,"

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.430 size:81% position:41% line:92%
as well you should be.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.999 line:92%
How was your Emmy experience?

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.434 line:92%
-Well, you know, you're very

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
philosophical
and calm and relaxed,

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
right up until about
2 minutes before

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
they call your name --
or don't...

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:22.542 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:25.411
-...and for about 5 minutes
afterwards, if they don't,

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're busy scrambling
to be philosophical,

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:32.552
you know, and see whether or not
you're believable when you,

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Oh, yeah.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, no.
That's a great choice.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:40.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
I told you."
You know, that kind of stuff.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we waited for
the commercial to be polite.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they have seat fillers,
so no one knows --

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
First off, no one
even knows you're there,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause we're all
so self-absorbed.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:51.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You know, it doesn't matter.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:54.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we --
Or at least this one is.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:55.575 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So, we got up and went

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:59.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
to this great restaurant
in downtown L.A.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.114 line:92%
-So that was it. You were out.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-7:00,
I was fairly well-hammered

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:06.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a couple of tequilas
with Mary,

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:10.490
you know, and went home,
and we were in bed by 9:00.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.991 line:92%
Just had the best evening.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:12.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's amazing.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:17.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say it is --
With the Creative Arts Emmys,

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:20.366
which is the week before,
our writing staff was nominated,

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was the first award
of a three-hour night.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
And our writing --
I wasn't there,

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
but our whole
writing staff was there.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.941 line:92%
And they announced it. We lost.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, immediately, one of
the guys --

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Coughing ] Loser.
Sorry.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:34.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no, that's fine.
It's fine.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, I wasn't there.
-No, no, no, no.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:40.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I wasn't a sucker
who actually went.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.958 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey!
-Hey!

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.561 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We are friends!

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know who else was
a sucker was --

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
Larry David was sitting right
in front of me.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.834
-Well that was --
I will say I really enjoyed it,

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:55.501 size:88% position:44% line:92%
'cause there was a shot.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was aware you were there
because, oh, you know,

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:58.538 line:92%
I'm lucky enough to know you

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:01.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm lucky enough
to know Larry a little bit.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.141 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Did Larry stay?

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would assume
he would also leave.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.145
-I think he had to do a bit.
-Oh, he did have to do a bit.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He had to present.
-He had to present.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Now, that's the true sucker.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:11.384 line:92%
-So he didn't get home until...

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:14.487 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, that is like --
So, you stay, you lose,

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you
still have to do stuff.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When he came up right before
the show started,

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:21.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
he goes --
he looked at me and went,

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:24.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You and I have a
1-in-100 chance of winning."

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.199 line:92%
I went, "That's not true,"

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
harboring the thought
that I might win.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.336 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was right.
-Yeah.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:33.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, you were like,
"That's not true, Larry.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.775 line:92%
You have a 1-in-100 chance."

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.809 line:92%
I want to mention "Cheers"

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:39.746
and I want to talk to you more
to you after the commercial.

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:40.413 size:75% position:38% line:92%
But "The Good Place"

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:43.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
had a fantastic
season finale at Season 2.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:47.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Are you watching?

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:51.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there was
a wonderful moment.

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:53.559
And, obviously, the creator
of the show, Mike Schur,

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:57.964
is a huge "Cheers" fan, as are
millions and millions of people.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he put you back
behind the bar.

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:02.168 size:78% position:39%
Your character got to
stand behind the bar.

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.736 size:75% position:38%
And for anyone who's
a fan of television,

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:06.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was a -- You know, it was
a real goose-bumps moment.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:09.409
Did you feel immediately natural
being behind the bar again?

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:11.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Okay.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:11.744 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, seriously.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:17.083
It took me a year and a half of
playing "Cheers," Sam Malone.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
My voice changed just now.
I'm starting to quaver.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:24.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm getting nervous and sick.
I never went to bars.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:29.228
I was the guy who -- I never
picked up women kind of thing.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:32.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
The woman would have to be
standing naked in front of me,

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.168 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and I would go, "Me?"

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.770 line:92%
So playing Sam Malone was an

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
anathema to me
for the longest time.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
So going back was --
All of a sudden,

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:45.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was full of insecurity and
just felt horrible.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:45.978 line:92%
-It did not look horrible,

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I guess that's
acting right there, yeah.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:51.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, you can --
If you watch the scene,

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:54.654
you'll notice that I would try
to remember, "What did I do?

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.356 line:92%
Oh, I used wash shot glasses.

00:05:56.356 --> 00:06:00.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. And then I have
a towel over my shoulder.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.061 line:92%
Yeah, I'll do the towel thing."

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:05.398
And you can see the towel
come up and down like 40 times.

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:06.733
-It's actually funny.
I had never thought about that.

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:11.504
But when you said, Sam Malone
was always washing shot glasses.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:12.138 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That seems like --

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:15.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't think anyone
on that show ever did a shot.

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:18.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. Beer.
-Beer. Everybody drank beer.

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:19.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I went to bartender school

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:23.082
and worked my little butt off
to learn how to make drinks.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:25.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the first month
of shooting, I was making

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:28.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
Manhattans and grasshoppers
and all sorts of weird drinks.

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:31.891
And then it dawned on me, they
didn't give a [bleep] about --

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:36.896
They want their jokes said well
and on time, you know?

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're shooting you
above your hands,

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:40.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
so all you see is this,
so I went...

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the towel.
We all loved the towel.

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:43.770 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was so great.

